# Working notes

## Brief: "~70% Shopify + UCP, capabilities vary"

**Shopify (~84 of 120 brands).** Every Shopify store exposes the same public product data, whatever the theme:
- `/products/<handle>.js` (or `.json`) gives every variant: id, options, `price`, `compare_at_price` (the crossed-out price).
- The product page embeds the same data (JSON-LD / product JSON).
- `?variant=<id>` pins the page to one variant.

**UCP (Universal Commerce Protocol).** An open agentic-commerce standard (Google + Shopify, early 2026). A merchant publishes a profile at `/.well-known/ucp` listing its capabilities (catalog, checkout, ...). Written from memory, so confirm it against the live sites before relying on it.

**"Capabilities vary", meaning the JSON isn't always the truth:**
- Apps can rewrite prices on the page (sale banners, "members save 20%", promo pop-ups), so the JSON and the visible page can disagree.
- Headless stores (a custom frontend over Shopify) may not serve the standard URLs.
- Some stores block or rate-limit `.js`/`.json`.

**Design implication:**

| Segment | Approach | Cost |
|---|---|---|
| Shopify/UCP (~84) | One shared adapter, structured data/UCP first, browser to confirm variant + price on the page | Cheap, one codebase |
| Long tail (~36) | Browser automation or ops review, per brand, by volume | Expensive, per-brand upkeep |

Caveat: 70% counts brands, not volume. Check which of the top-12 brands are on Shopify. West Elm, CB2, Crate & Barrel and RH are likely custom stacks (unverified).

## Sample: Lulu and Georgia, Carson Sofa (`carson-sofa.js`)

**Recorded evidence**, not a live observation. File saved 2026-11-10 22:02 local; the fetch time isn't inside the file.
- Source: `https://www.luluandgeorgia.com/products/carson-sofa.js`. Confirms **Lulu and Georgia is Shopify** and the endpoint is public.
- Product id `7553558872163`, vendor "Lulu and Georgia", type Furniture.
- Options: **Color** (25 fabrics) x **Size** (`85"W`, `103"W`, `120"W`), giving **75 variants**, all `available: true`.
- **Prices are integer cents**: `259800` = $2,598.00. Range $1,898–$2,898.
- **Price varies by size AND fabric**, which makes this a good product for proving the right variant was picked:
  - 85"W: $1,898 / $2,098 / $2,298
  - 103"W: $2,198 / $2,398 / $2,598
  - 120"W: $2,498 / $2,698 / $2,898
- `compare_at_price == price` on every variant, so **no strike-through sale** at capture. Rule: a sale only when `compare_at_price > price`; equal or null means none.
- No selling plans, no quantity price breaks, `quantity_rule` min 1 / increment 1, so unit price x qty is safe for this product.
- Example variants:
  - `42487540056163` Ivory Modern Boucle / 103"W, $2,598, SKU L0484640
  - `42487540088931` Balsam Classic Velvet / 103"W, $2,398, SKU L0484641

**What the JSON can't tell us** (this is why we need the browser step):
- Membership-only or promo-code prices. These live in on-page banners/apps, not in `.js`.
- Whether the rendered page shows the same price for the selected variant.
- Market/currency. `.js` reflects the storefront's context. Pin a US/USD context and record it.

## Live checks, 2026-11-10 16:39–16:42 UTC (current observations, this run)

**UCP, Lulu and Georgia: present.** `GET /.well-known/ucp` returns 200 JSON, version `2026-08-25`, MCP endpoint `https://lulu-and-georgia.myshopify.com/api/ucp/mcp`.
- Capabilities: checkout, fulfillment, discount, cart, buyer_consent, order, catalog.search, **catalog.lookup**, dev.shopify.catalog, location.*, identity_linking, permalink, ask, declared_fields.
- `catalog.lookup` is a likely structured price source to try next to `.js`. `fulfillment` + `cart` may cover the optional shipping quote. Not exercised yet.
- My earlier "written from memory" note on UCP is now confirmed for this site.

**UCP, Nordic Knots: absent.** `/.well-known/ucp` returns the site's HTML app, not a profile.

**Nordic Knots is NOT standard Shopify.** It's headless Next.js on Vercel:
- `server: Vercel`, cookies `NEXT_COUNTRY=US`, `NEXT_LANGUAGE=en`, redirects `/` to `/us`.
- `/us/products.json` returns the app's JSON error, not Shopify data. No `myshopify`/`cdn.shopify` reference found.
- So it lands in the "inconsistent infrastructure" bucket. This is the **brief's "capabilities vary" in practice**, and it's an argument that the 70% figure must be checked per brand.

**BLOCKER: every Nordic Knots page returns an error.** `/us`, `/us/rugs/...` and `/us/collections/all` return HTTP **200** with body `{"error":"Internal Server Error","status":500}`, in both curl **and** a real Chrome tab.
- Static routes work: `robots.txt` and `/api/sitemap/us` (1,896 URLs) return 200.
- The Vercel edge was `bom1` (Mumbai). Likely a geo or edge problem from India, or a real outage. Unverified.
- **Lesson for validation: HTTP 200 is not success.** The body must parse as the expected shape, or the result is unresolved.
- Next: retry later, or try a US egress. If it's still blocked, ship Nordic Knots as an **unresolved result with this evidence** (the brief allows "document blocker, move on").

**Lulu and Georgia `.js` rate-limited.** The re-fetch of `carson-sofa.js` at 16:42 UTC returned **429**, empty body, a few minutes after the first fetch plus the UCP probe.
- So a variant re-check can't be a tight loop.
- Needs: backoff, a cache with an observation time, and UCP/page as the fallback source.
- Good candidate for the **month-1 priority / observed limitation** in the write-up.


## Replacement brand scan (live, 2026-11-10 17:00 UTC, one `/products.json?limit=1` per site)

| Brand | Response | Read |
|---|---|---|
| Parachute, Jenni Kayne, Sundays, Sabai, House of Leon | 429 `local_rate_limited` (text/plain) | Shopify edge throttle, so **likely Shopify** |
| Serena & Lily | 404, Next.js HTML | Headless, no Shopify JSON |
| Italic | 404, Next.js HTML | Headless |
| Soho Home | 403 Cloudflare "Just a moment..." | Bot challenge |

**Key finding: Shopify rate-limits per client IP across ALL stores.** Five unrelated stores returned the same `local_rate_limited` on their **first** request.
- The earlier L&G 429 is most likely the same throttle, not L&G-specific.
- Architecture impact: one shared, global request budget for all ~84 Shopify brands, not per-brand limits. Plus a cache, and a cooldown after a 429.
- Strong month-1 item.

Headless (Nordic Knots, Serena & Lily, Italic) and Cloudflare (Soho Home) are a real pattern even among named brands, not edge cases.

