## Serena & Lily check (live, 2026-11-10 17:10–17:12 UTC), PICKED as the Nordic Knots substitute

**Platform matches Nordic Knots:**
- `server: Vercel`, same `bom1` edge as Nordic Knots, Next.js (`__NEXT_DATA__`, ~750 KB).
- No `myshopify`/`cdn.shopify` reference. `/products.json` returns 404.
- **UCP absent:** `/.well-known/ucp` returns 404 (Next.js HTML).

**Difference from Nordic Knots (why it's usable):**
- curl gets **403** (bot challenge HTML), but a **real Chrome tab renders the pages**.
- So browser automation is required here, not optional. That makes it the brief's "browser-dependent flow".

**Product:** Delancey Quilt. Links:
- Product base: https://www.serenaandlily.com/products/delancey-quilt/1358964
  - **Redirects to a default variant** (`/1359007`, Full/Queen, Grove).
  - Never treat the landing URL as the requested variant. Always confirm the selected size+color on the page.
- Full/Queen, Coastal Blue: https://www.serenaandlily.com/products/delancey-quilt/1358963
- Full/Queen, Grove: https://www.serenaandlily.com/products/delancey-quilt/1359007
- Master (no complete variant): https://www.serenaandlily.com/products/delancey-quilt/m16292

**Options:** Size {Full/Queen, King/Cal King} x Color {Coastal Blue, Lark, Grove, Blush}.

**Prices (rendered DOM, client-side):**

| Variant | Original (compare-at) | Selling | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| Full/Queen (Grove, Coastal Blue) | $448 | **$268** | "Save 40%" |
| King/Cal King | $498 | $298 | Implied by the range "$448 - $498" / "$268 - $298 (Save up to 40%)" |

- Sizes ARE priced differently, so the variant choice is provable.
- A **live sale** is good for showing selling vs compare-at.
- The compare-at isn't styled `line-through` in CSS. It's two separate `<h5>` elements, so tell them apart by order/class + the "Save X%" text, not by strike-through.
- Banner "Sale of the Year. Best Pricing + Free Shipping": **sitewide, no code needed**, so it's not promo-code pricing. Record it as evidence.
- Affirm "$24/mo" is a financing figure. It must be ignored, never taken as the price.

**Gotchas seen:**
- King/Cal King was **unavailable** in Grove and Coastal Blue.
  - Clicking it in Grove cleared the color, moved to master `m16292`, showed only the range, and said "We only have 0 of those available".
  - Rule: an incomplete selection or range-only price = **unresolved**, never the lower end of the range.
- No price found in `__NEXT_DATA__` (key scan). Price arrives client-side. The source API isn't identified yet (network capture started too late).
- One scripted color click didn't register (page stayed on Coastal Blue). Variant selection must re-read the selected options after each action, not assume.

**Input-file proposal:** Delancey Quilt, Full/Queen, Coastal Blue, qty 1. URL `/products/delancey-quilt/1358963`. Expected selling price **$268** (compare-at $448).
- Optional failure demo: request King/Cal King / Coastal Blue → unresolved (unavailable, range-only).

